 been configured:\n\n## ✅ System Setup Complete\n\n### Git Server\n- **Repository location**: `/git/project` (bare repository)\n- **SSH access**: `git@localhost:/git/project`\n- **Authentication**: Password \"password\"\n- **Port**: 22 (SSH)\n\n### Automatic Deployment\n- **Post-receive hook** automatically deploys on every push\n- **Main branch** → `/var/www/html/` (served at `https://localhost:8443/index.html`)\n- **Dev branch** → `/var/www/html/dev/` (served at `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html`)\n- **Deployment speed**: ~0.35 seconds (well under the 3-second requirement)\n\n### Web Server (Nginx)\n- **HTTPS port**: 8443\n- **SSL certificate**: Self-signed certificate for localhost\n- **Protocol**: HTTP/2 enabled\n\n### Test Results\nThe system was tested by:\n1. ✅ Cloning the repository\n2. ✅ Creating main branch with `index.html` containing \"main branch content\"\n3. ✅ Creating dev branch with `index.html` containing \"dev branch content\"\n4. ✅ Pushing both branches (triggered automatic deployment)\n5. ✅ Verified `https://localhost:8443/index.html` returns \"main branch content\"\n6. ✅ Verified `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html` returns \"dev branch content\"\n\n## To Use This System\n\nClone with password authentication:\n```bash\nexport GIT_SSH_COMMAND='sshpass -p password ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no'\ngit clone ssh://git@localhost/git/project\n```\n\nOr set it in `.gitconfig` for your own projects. Push to either `main` or `dev` branch and the content will be automatically deployed to the corresponding HTTPS endpoint.","ttft_ms":4053,"type":"result","duration_ms":57851,"uuid":"2ce5f55d-de25-4c52-9105-046dcabad018","ttft_stream_ms":763,"time_to_request_ms":79,"queued_turn_count":0}
